# Atlas Engineering OS Governance Rules

## 1. Blueprint First Mandate
Always inspect `.atlas/blueprint.yaml` before making architectural or code modifications.

## 2. Anti-Bloat Decision Ladder (Ponytail Protocol)
Before generating or modifying any code, pass the request through this decision ladder:
1. STEP 1 (YAGNI): Is this abstraction or helper strictly necessary right now? If speculative, DO NOT implement it.
2. STEP 2 (Native First): Prefer built-in language capabilities or existing framework features over custom helper modules.
3. STEP 3 (Single-Line Rule): If logic can be expressed clearly in 1–2 inline statements, do NOT create a dedicated helper function or file.
4. STEP 4 (Refactor over Expansion): Modify existing files instead of spawning new files or factory structures.
5. STEP 5 (Justification Gate): Document inline architectural justification if creating a new file is unavoidable.
